Package: figspec
Title: Check and Export Figures Against Journal Submission Requirements
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Daniel", "Semakula, MD, MPH, PhD",
           email = "semakuladaniel@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Academic journals publish precise requirements for submitted
    figures: column widths, minimum resolution, permitted file formats,
    minimum type size and colour mode. These requirements are scattered across
    publisher websites and are easy to miss until a manuscript reaches
    production. 'figspec' provides a curated, source-referenced registry of
    those requirements, a theme and export helper that applies them to
    'ggplot2' figures, and a checker that reports where a figure would fail.
    Every registry entry records the publisher page it was taken from and the
    date it was verified, and requirements a publisher does not state are
    reported as unspecified rather than assumed to pass.
